\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0      O! my Lord Jesus, what are
\par         you accused of?
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj  That made your kinsmen to condemn
\par you to death?
\par  What at all is it? which is so unheard of
\par  to merit such judgement?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.   You were so stripped, given a crown of thorns
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj  slapped in the face and spat upon your body
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  given a sour drink, stretched your arms on the cross
\par  and crucified you there.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.   What was the basis for all this wickedness
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj  Truly my sins were put on you in my stead
\par  My Lord, Jesus, I am the cause of all this
\par  I am the offender.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  4.     I am greatly surprised at this punishment
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj  You the caretaker was killed for your sheep
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  You the Lord allowed the servants penalty
\par  To be pronounced on you.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.    Because of your great love which you have for me
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj  that you came to suffer in my stead
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  I fancy too much this world's worthless things
\par  and this brought you trouble.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6.    Saviour how shall I express my thanksfullness?
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj  How shall I befittingly praise your love?
\par  It's higher than my thoughts and my lip praises
\par  O! what shall I do?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7.     I just don't know what I shall do to please you
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  I'll have to forego my many desires
\par  I will not allow myself to be in sin
\par  to sin against you.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8.    I'll hang all my desires there on the cross
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj  even that is not within my own power
\par  therefore I plead with you through your Holy Spirit
\par  to come and strengthen me.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9.    Let me survey your love and abundant grace
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  and not trust in things of this vain wild world
\par  but make the effort to pursue things that will
\par  help me to love you more.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10.   I will follow you, I am your disciple
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj  and will not have regard for people's disgrace
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  If they trouble me, let me stand very firm
\par  and not deny you.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 11\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 11.  All these are minors and not very much
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0  I know that my Redeemer won't reject me
\par  Receive whate'er I have which I am giving
\par Receive my heart too.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-315\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 12\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 12. My master Jesus, you who're with the Father
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 If one day I would be before your throne
\par I would also wear your kingly crown and sing
\par and praise you always.
\par \pard\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

